Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 13:41:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 041/154] feat: auto-peek goes, shift+click peek comes back
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Peek had two triggers and the cut hit them differently.

Auto-peek asked Swift one question - is this tab pinned or favourited - and
nothing else could answer it. The throttle, ShouldAutoPeek and the posted
open go. A follow-up rebuilds the trigger against the Rust core, which owns
the spaces model now.

Shift+click is the opposite. Its whole implementation is C++ and survived
intact; the only thing stopping it was `connected() && peek_connected()` in
Browser::OpenURLFromTab, which has been false since the cut. Dropping those
two lines gives the feature back.

atrium_peek_decision stays with its gtest suite. It is the Keyhole promise
- a pinned page never navigates away - written as a testable
rule, and the rebuild starts from it.

Kept, and easy to sweep by mistake: the throttle's note that peek must never
open synchronously from inside a throttle callback, because NavigationRequest
re-enters. That is a constraint on the rebuild, not dylib behaviour, so it is
recorded for that follow-up.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
